07","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For independent uniform variables on $(0,1)$, find the second moment $\\mathbb{E}[(X+Y)^2]$ of their sum.","options":["$1$","$\\tfrac{7}{6}$","$\\tfrac{2}{3}$","$\\tfrac{4}{3}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1ac44d4fbeadcfcff94ca6dc","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For independent $\\operatorname{Unif}(0,1)$ variables $X$ and $Y$, compute $\\mathbb{E}[\\max(X,Y)]$.","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{3}$","$\\tfrac{3}{4}$","$\\tfrac{2}{3}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d609d06e88142d3c077585a0","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Two independent $\\operatorname{Unif}(0,1)$ variables $X$ and $Y$ are drawn. What is the expected distance $\\mathbb{E}|X-Y|$ between them?","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{3}$","$0$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{6}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0fb4d343f97417f2ea66c46d","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Independent $X,Y\\sim\\operatorname{Unif}(0,1)$ are combined into $X\\mathrm{e}^Y$. Compute its mean.","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{2}\\mathrm{e}^{1/2}$","$\\mathrm{e}-1$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}(\\mathrm{e}-1)$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e8eb0df6042ea1cb041587de","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the disc $x^2+y^2<1$. Writing $r=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$, which integral gives $\\mathbb{E}[X^2+Y^2]$?","options":["$\\int_0^1r^2\\,\\mathrm{d}r$","$\\int_0^1r^2\\cdot2r\\,\\mathrm{d}r$","$\\int_0^1r^2\\cdot\\tfrac{1}{\\pi}\\,\\mathrm{d}r$","$\\int_{-1}^1\\int_{-1}^1(x^2+y^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7f0631b560ad7dbd16a28f28","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A jointly continuous pair $(X,Y)$ has finite second moments. A student claims that LOTUS gives $\\mathbb{E}[XY]=\\mathbb{E}[X]\\mathbb{E}[Y]$ only when $X$ and $Y$ are independent. Which assessment is correct?","options":["The claim is correct: equality of this moment forces the joint density to factorise.","The claim is false: this moment equality can also hold for a dependent pair.","The claim is correct: every dependent pair necessarily has nonzero covariance.","The claim is false: the moment equality holds for every jointly continuous pair."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"36098acc2d2c3709e9d06e0f","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A pair $(X,Y)$ has joint density $f_{X,Y}$ supported on a set $S\\subseteq\\{(x,y)\\colon y>0\\}$. Assume $\\iint_S |x/y|f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y<\\infty$. Which expression computes $\\mathbb{E}[X/Y]$ directly, without deriving the ratio's density?","options":["$\\iint_S (x/y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\displaystyle\\frac{\\iint_S xf_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y}{\\iint_S yf_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y}$","$\\iint_S (x/y)f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\iint_S (y/x)f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"67cddff91281a56ce7914ebe","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have density $6x$ on $0<x<y<1$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[XY]$?","options":["$\\tfrac{3}{8}$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$","$\\tfrac{2}{5}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b61d30bbaa767774dba06b1d","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A pair $(X,Y)$ has a joint density and finite first absolute moments. Which condition is necessary and sufficient for $\\mathbb{E}[\\max(X,Y)]=\\max(\\mathbb{E}[X],\\mathbb{E}[Y])$?","options":["One variable is at least the other with probability one.","The two variables have equal finite expectations.","The joint density is the product of the two marginal densities.","The joint density is invariant under exchanging the coordinates."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c7982009b347078d67391692","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"$(X,Y)$ has density $1/12$ on $-2<x<2$, $0<y<3$, and zero elsewhere. Define $g(x,y)=1/x$ for $x\\ne0$ and $g(0,y)=0$. Symmetrically excluding $|x|<\\varepsilon$ gives an integral of zero for every $0<\\varepsilon<2$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[g(X,Y)]$?","options":["Zero, because the symmetrically truncated integrals are zero.","$+\\infty$, because the positive part has infinite expectation.","$-\\infty$, because the negative part has infinite expectation.","Undefined, because both parts have infinite expectation."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"79cec3a4405369bffbfd1c21","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_lotus_two_dimensional_continuous_7fc24287_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the disc $x^2+y^2<1$, and $R=\\sqrt{X^2+Y^2}$. Define $H=1/R$ when $R>0$ and $H=0$ when $R=0$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[H]$?","options":["$+\\infty$","$\\tfrac{3}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{\\pi}$","$2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3217a9a5089f7bae98e7476d","time_limit":40}]}}